{
 "note": "Levels (PLAN.md section 2). ask = names as in world.json, continents, or islands below. pick = how many to ask (at random) when ask is longer. camera: 'globe' (whole globe turned to the answer), 'continent' (each question flies to the answer's continent), 'level' (one view for the whole level: region key or {lon, lat, ext}), 'island' (a wide view of the ocean with the island off-centre). pale: countries not asked (and not home) are drawn pale. flags: how many questions show five flags. Without lightup, each is about a country already found in the trip (the painted flags are hidden meanwhile, so it's remembering, not matching); with lightup the country lights up unfound. cards: how the four wrong flags are chosen: far (other continents), near (same continent), alike (look-alike flags first). dev/voices.py renders the question lines for every name asked here. regions: the camera's view of each continent (centre and half-width in degrees). closer: a place smaller than minPx on the shorter side of a phone (360 px), outside the planned view, or on an island level, gets a view of its own: view[0] times its size, at least view[1] and at most view[2] degrees each way, wide on purpose so it isn't the obvious answer, the place pushed off-centre by up to offset of the view (children can pinch to zoom in). tour: the endless World tour after level 12; most questions come from the passport, `new` of them from the places not stamped yet (its ask list adds countries no level asks). capitals: each country's capital city, with where it is (for the star); a level with capitals: true asks every question as \"Find the country with the capital city …\", and a number asks that many of a trip's questions that way (only for countries listed here).",
